From 35f0bf8f174b297addc4216454f07fa5ed7d0aa5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 05:24:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Priorities: move onto the page structure (PrioritiesPage
 + PrioritiesPageContext)

The route is an adapter: it reads the matrix and shapes it with toPrioritiesPageProps(matrix, today) (the no-plan week fallback moves out of the route), then renders PrioritiesPage. PriorityMatrixPage becomes PrioritiesPage and absorbs PrioritiesScreen, rendering BoardHeader itself. The container provides PrioritiesPageContext (activePlanId, the open popover, overlay openers and the track/complete writes), so QuadrantCell, MatrixTaskCard, MoveToPopover, MoveToRows and the mobile sheet take their rows as props and no callback props. groupTasksByQuadrant and isTrackedTask in oneOffUtils replace the container's grouping and the duplicated tracked checks; FALLBACK_QUADRANT moves there with them. Unit tests cover the adapter and both helpers.

Design Console: the matrix tabs render PrioritiesPage with raw matrix fixtures passed through the route's adapter; the MatrixTaskCard specimen and the mobile sheet panel render inside inertPrioritiesPageContext(activePlanId), tracked when the task's planId is the active plan.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KCt6pLLUiRAHZu45QycSRC
